[00:37.03] As the evening sun goes down
[00:40.75] The Dealer shuffles into town
[00:44.98] Makes a note of what's a float
[00:48.64] And spinning 'round he'll cut your throat
[00:52.38] In the time it takes to heal
[00:54.95] The dealer's made another deal
[00:59.24] When he plays he plays for keeps
[01:02.99] And sweeps the spinning roulette wheel
[01:06.79] Dealer, Dealer
[01:12.76] Like the mighty ocean's roar
[01:15.14] He gets all his share and more
[01:16.82] Mexican right to the core and very proud
[01:21.24] He'll get even with the score
[01:25.47] Leave your wife a weeping widow on the shore
[01:55.86] Between the desert and the dove
[01:58.86] Money is his only love
[02:03.31] Feeling nothing deep inside
[02:06.47] His mind is governed by his pride
[02:10.41] In a smoky little room
[02:13.59] Shadows moving in the gloom
[02:17.07] Someone turns a running flush
[02:20.49] And breaks the deathly quiet hush
[02:24.07] Dealer, Dealer
